        "text_matches": [
          {
            "property": "content",
            "fragment": "\nFor every divisor d of n with n at least two, rational sigma coordinates realize the values obtained by subtracting n times the order-class indicator from the totient of d and dividing by two. The coordinates are Ramanujan sums, with the middle coordinate halved when n is even. The public divisor-sum identity proves integrality by induction on the modulus. Finite geometric sums then give the full Fourier transform: n on primitive roots of order d and zero elsewhere. Removing the constant coefficient subtracts the totient of d. Coefficient reconstruction pairs reciprocal exponents and accounts for the doubled middle monomial.\n",
            "matches": [
              {
                "text": "Ramanujan",
                "indices": [
                  214,
                  223
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
